/P 133 0 R
/T (Figure 3 shows the sources of the contributions that UNAIDS received, disaggregated by the US, the EU27 countries, and the rest of the world. While the US remains the largest individual contributor to the organization, its contributions have been gradually scaled back since 2020. As of 2023, US resources account for one-third of UNAIDS contributions. In contrast, EU27 countries have now become the largest collective donor to the organization: in 2016, EU27 contributions accounted for 30% of the total contributions received, while in 2023 they stand at 43%. )
/E (Figure 3 shows the sources of the contributions that UNAIDS received, disaggregated by the US, the EU27 countries, and the rest of the world. While the US remains the largest individual contributor to the organization, its contributions have been gradually scaled back since 2020. As of 2023, US resources account for one-third of UNAIDS contributions. In contrast, EU27 countries have now become the largest collective donor to the organization: in 2016, EU27 contributions accounted for 30% of the total contributions received, while in 2023 they stand at 43%. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
